#. Tag: title
#: getkde.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting &kde;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I get &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main distribution site for &kde; is <ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.kde.org/"
"\">ftp.kde.org</ulink>. However, this site is often under heavy load, so you "
"might prefer to use <ulink url=\"http://download.kde.org/\">download.kde."
"org</ulink> which automatically redirects you to the mirror nearest to you. "
"You can also have a look at the list of <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org/"
"ftpmirrors.html\"> &kde; mirror sites</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Are there &Linux; distributions that include &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes, major &Linux; distributions already ship &kde;. As building a "
"distribution takes some time, they might not always contain the latest "
"version, but for a start or to avoid downloading from the Internet, they do "
"provide a good starting point."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find an up-to-date list of distributions that ship with &kde; <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.kde.org/download/distributions.php\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is the current version?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Currently, the latest stable version is 3.5.5"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org/info/3.5.5.php\">&kde; 3.5.5 Info Page</"
"ulink> contains a lot of information specific to this release."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I find &kde; snapshots?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can get the latest snapshots from <ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/"
"unstable/snapshots\">ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/unstable/snapshots</ulink>. "
"You might also want to consider setting up your own <acronym>SVN</acronym> "
"client in order to maintain the latest snapshot at all times. Please refer "
"to <ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org/source/anonsvn.html\">Anonymous "
"<acronym>SVN</acronym> and &kde;</ulink> for further information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I get &Qt;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&Qt; is a product of the Norwegian company Trolltech. You can always get the "
"latest &Qt; version from their <ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.trolltech.com\">&FTP; "
"server</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And with most up-to-date &Linux; distributions, &Qt; is already included. "
"Please see <xref linkend=\"prerequisites\"/> for the version of &Qt; you "
"need."
msgstr ""

